From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 02:34:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] device/Kconfig: Allow a dGPU VBIOS without an iGPU VBIOS

VGA_BIOS_DGPU depends on VGA_BIOS, so the VBIOS of a discrete GPU can
only be added together with one for the integrated GPU. On boards that
initialize the iGPU natively, that image is never used, and VGA_BIOS
also selects VGA_ROM_RUN_DEFAULT, which switches the default graphics
init from libgfxinit to running option ROMs. For example, a config for
lenovo/w541 with only the NVIDIA VBIOS silently drops it, so the GPU
gets no _ROM method, while adding an Intel VBIOS to keep it changes
the graphics init.

The CBFS file of the dGPU image does not depend on VGA_BIOS, so drop
the Kconfig dependency.

TEST=olddefconfig for lenovo/w541 with only VGA_BIOS_DGPU keeps it and
libgfxinit. With both VGA_BIOS and VGA_BIOS_DGPU, the result does not
change. Built lenovo/w541 with only the NVIDIA VBIOS and checked that
pci10de,11fc.rom is in CBFS.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/device/Kconfig | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/device/Kconfig b/src/device/Kconfig
index f3a3ef7be..33e8306c5 100644
--- a/src/device/Kconfig
+++ b/src/device/Kconfig
@@ -918,11 +918,16 @@ config VGA_BIOS_SECOND_ID
 
 config VGA_BIOS_DGPU
 	bool "Add a discrete VGA BIOS image"
-	depends on VGA_BIOS
+	depends on ARCH_X86
 	help
 	  Select this option if you have a VGA BIOS image for discrete GPU
 	  that you would like to add to your ROM.
 
+	  This does not need a VGA BIOS for the integrated GPU. Boards that
+	  initialize it natively, e.g. with libgfxinit, can add only the
+	  discrete GPU image, which the OS can then read through the ACPI
+	  _ROM method of the GPU.
+
 	  You will be able to specify the location and file name of the
 	  image later.
 
-- 
